 from across your entire security ecosystem to provide a 360-degree view of risk within a single, intuitive interface. Built for Enterprise Safety & Scalability The SafeBreach CTEM Platform was built for Fortune 500 and Global 2000 environments. It meets the stringent safety and privacy requirements of the world’s most mature security programs and is backed by an award-winning customer success team. Frequently Asked Questions Have a question about the SafeBreach CTEM Platform? We’re here to help. What is the SafeBreach CTEM Platform and how does it work? The SafeBreach Continuous Threat Exposure Management (CTEM) Platform is designed to help organizations move from reactive security to a proactive, closed-loop risk management program. It utilizes the new SafeBreach Helm AI infrastructure layer—and three purpose-built AI agents—to operationalize the five-phased CTEM framework. The platform empowers organizations to continuously identify, prioritize, and remediate cyber risk at scale. How does SafeBreach Helm simplify CTEM operations? Rather than navigating multiple dashboards or manually correlating data across tools, security teams can simply ask Helm a single question using plain language—for example: “Where could Volt Typhoon threat actors gain traction in my environment and what gaps should I fix first?” Helm automatically interprets the query, dispatches the appropriate AI agents to gather and analyze the relevant data, and returns one coordinated, actionable response. Security leaders get faster answers and security teams get seamlessly executed remediation workflows to quickly mitigate the most critical exposures. What role does Adversarial Exposure Validation (AEV) play in CTEM? SafeBreach Helm and the SafeBreach CTEM Platform are designed to work with your existing security stack, including integrations with Vulnerability Management (VM) platforms, External Attack Surface Management (EASM) solutions, Threat Intelligence (TI) feeds, Security Orchestration, Automation, and Response",
